WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.671
Behind the charter sit fifteen
principles, in five groups,

2
00:00:03.671 --> 00:00:06.462
each tied to the book
that carries it in depth.

3
00:00:06.462 --> 00:00:10.706
The foundation group applies to
every change: one source of truth,

4
00:00:10.706 --> 00:00:14.163
change control with provenance,
and drift detection.

5
00:00:14.163 --> 00:00:16.237
The change rule is the strict one.

6
00:00:16.237 --> 00:00:21.165
Every move, add, change, deletion or
reset starts at the source of truth,

7
00:00:21.165 --> 00:00:26.091
carries a real authorization, runs
with just-in-time least privilege,

8
00:00:26.091 --> 00:00:30.413
closes with proof, and produces
its evidence automatically.

9
00:00:30.413 --> 00:00:34.138
Put simply, no closure counts
unless it carries its proof.

10
00:00:34.138 --> 00:00:39.219
The other groups say what replaces the
OU tree, how devices and policy move,

11
00:00:39.219 --> 00:00:43.800
how the HR feed and SQL Server fit
in, and how the program itself runs.

12
00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.382
Two source rules were also corrected
against Microsoft's documentation,

13
00:00:48.382 --> 00:00:51.837
including token lifetimes;
the details are in the notes.

14
00:00:51.837 --> 00:00:54.020
Next, the phases and gates.
